                <pb facs="0216" n="142" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg142"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pontifical Telegraph.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[Presented at <placeName>Velletri</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-11-08">8th November, 1866</date>, at
                        8.35 a. m. Received at Rome 8th November, 1866, at 8.50 a.
                    m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>His Excellency the <hi rendition="#small-caps">General,</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister of War, Rome:</hi></p>
                <p>I received the following telegram, dated ——, from Captain Lambilly:</p>
                <p>At the moment of leaving the prison, surrounded by six men as guards, Watson
                    plunged into the ravine, more than a hundred feet deep, which defends the
                    prison. Fifty zouaves are in pursuit. I will send your excellency the news which
                    I shall receive by telegraph.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lieutenant Colonel</hi>
                    ALLET.</signed></closer>
            </div>
